TEXT -448 -224 Left 2 ;Common emitter vs common source: the same supply, collector/drain resistor (4.7k), emitter/source resistor (1k, bypassed by CE/CS) and load (RL = 10k), both at about 1.4 mA.\nAv = −gm (RC ∥ RL). The BJT has gm = IC/VT ≈ 55 mS: Av ≈ −160 (44 dB). The MOSFET has gm = √(2 Kp ID) ≈ 8 mS: Av ≈ −25 (28 dB). At the same current the BJT gives much more gain.\nThe gate draws no current, so the MOSFET's divider can be in megohms: Rin ≈ 690 kΩ, against ≈ 4.2 kΩ for the BJT (RB1 ∥ RB2 ∥ rπ). The bypass capacitor sees 1/gm, hence the low-frequency corner: ≈ 83 Hz and ≈ 14 Hz.\nWaveforms: with only 5 mV in, the BJT output is already a little asymmetric (vbe has to stay well below VT = 26 mV). Bias point: hover over Q1 and M1.
TEXT -256 -64 Left 2 ;BJT: BC547C
TEXT 576 -64 Left 2 ;MOSFET: 2N7000
